; Rule 1's tracker half. Two channels sound, so the skeleton states two
; bound `notes` lanes; channel 1's volume column MOVES (64, 48, 32), so
; it earns a bound `curve` as well. The module conducts: `:conductor` is
; the anchor, the tempo table is the timing walk's, and the bar grid
; comes from the highlight `[4 16]` — 16 rows to the measure over 4 to
; the beat, which is [4 4].
;
; `T80` on row 16 is a tempo change to 128, so the echo carries two
; segments and every position past row 16 is on the second one.
; The walk itself is `walk-*`'s business — this case asks the walk only
; for what a PLAYHEAD reads out of it, which is the `(order, row,
; tick-in-row)` beside every position below.
(read)
(dump)
(build :kind it)
(at :tick 0)
(at :tick 184504320)
(times "3FE0000000000000")
